this morning we do remember the longest  serving republican u.s senator in  history that would be orrin hatch he  died on saturday he was 88 years old  hatch represented utah and the state for  42 years spanning seven presidents from  jimmy carter to donald trump he  sponsored or co-sponsored more than 750  bills that later became law at the end  of his senate tenure hatch became a  staunch  ally rather president trump he also  played a vital role in crafting the  republicans  2017 tax cuts hatch was a reliable  conservative vote throughout his career  but he was also known for working with  democrats on issues like stem cell  research and expanding children's health  insurance before he retired in 2019  hatch issued a sharp warning about the  dangers of party politics listen to this  on both the left and the right  the bar of decency  has been set so low that jumping over it  is no longer the objective  limbo is the new name of the game  how low can you go  all the evidence points to an unsettling  truth  the senate as an institution  is in crisis or at least maybe in crisis  president biden who served in the senate  with hatch for 32 years said in the  statement that he was quote the fighter  who never humored a bully or shied away  from a challenge he was quite simply an  american original
 

